  "answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative aimed at revolutionizing the company's approach to the field. The project kicked off on June 15th with an initial budget of $500,000, led by Sarah Tan. Key milestones include the successful completion of the testing phase and the design phase, with a prototype for secure file sharing tested ahead of schedule. The project has expanded its team with new members Mike Chen and Lisa Ray, and is exploring partnerships with TechInnovate for AI technology. Budget updates indicate an adjustment to $550,000 due to unforeseen expenses, followed by a significant executive board approval of $2 million to cover all research, development, and marketing phases. The project is currently moving into the development phase under lead developer Omar Jensen, with upcoming security protocol updates and user interface enhancements planned."
